    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.x\n\n### Description\n\nAs the title describes, in TypeScript files, commenting lines won't add a space before the commented part, e.g.,\n\n```ts\ngetHello(): string {\n  return 'Hello World!';\n}\n```\n\nafter commenting\n\n```ts\n//getHello(): string {\n//  return 'Hello World!';\n//}\n```\n\nbut it is expected to be\n\n```ts\n// getHello(): string {\n//   return 'Hello World!';\n// }\n```\n\n### Reproduction\n\nI have created a repo at https://github.com/bowentan/kickstart.nvim with the branch `self` which is currently in use on my system.",
