        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "As @krovuxdev noticed, the reference branch indeed doesn't use 'mini.comment' at all. Instead it uses built-in commenting that is available since Neovim 0.10.0. It also uses 'commentstring' option to infer comment structure.\n\nIt so happens that default 'commentstring' value in Typescript files is \"//%s\" and built-in commenting uses it verbatim without padding (which is intended). The suggested solutions are:\n- Add `require('mini.comment').setup()` to use commenting from 'mini.comment' which *will* automatically pad comment parts (with default `config.option.pad_comment_parts`).\n- Set `vim.bo.commentstring = '// %s'` for files with 'typescript' filetype. Either in `FileType` autocommand or in '~/.config/nvim/after/ftplugin/typescript.lua'.\n- Update to Neovim 0.11 (current unstable nightly) which has padded commentstring by default.",
            "created_at": "2025-02-25T07:54:34Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1611#issuecomment-2681007470",
